domain ADR0030B4LocalVerification:
  description "Verify the local durable migration-attempt and preservation implementation."

problem P1:
  |
    Accepted ADR-0030 B4 requires frozen source and request identities,
    append-oriented persistence, restricted bounded preservation, disclosure
    controls, and crash/retry fixtures without crossing into semantic generation
    or activation.

evidence E_CONTRACT:
  |
    packages/shared/src/character-semantic-migration.ts defines strict JSON-only
    attempt, natural-source disclosure, request, accounting, receipt, event, and
    preservation-capsule contracts. It registers two disclosure contracts,
    requires disclosed paths to exactly match stored fragments, fixes the provider
    ceiling at six, and fixes the capsule ceiling at 256 KiB.

evidence E_PERSISTENCE:
  |
    backend/migrations/0024_character_semantic_migration.sql and the SQLite
    bootstrap add dedicated immutable attempt and provider-request bases,
    append-only events, one terminal receipt per provider request, and a separate
    content-digested capsule table bound to source and target generations.
    backend/src/repositories/character-semantic-migration.ts verifies source
    bytes, digest, schema, owner and current pointer before each new or replayed
    provider request, serializes same-attempt writes, rejects identity drift,
    and exposes capsule reads only through the registered remigration consumer.

evidence E_FIXTURES:
  |
    Six focused SQLite tests verify exact attempt and receipt replay, crash resume
    from an unreceipted request, failure followed by a separately identified
    request, six-request enforcement, disclosure rejection, capsule bounds,
    owner and consumer restrictions, current-pointer preservation, and pointer
    drift rejection before provider work. The tests make no provider call.

evidence E_GATES:
  |
    The final full run passed shared 334, backend 363, frontend 20, deployment 3,
    and release 5 tests. All workspace typechecks, production builds, duplicate
    detection, git diff check, and the targeted ADR-0030 check passed. Lizard
    1.23.0 checked 191 files and 3314 functions within unchanged baselines:
    complexity 117/121 with max 87/92, length 67/67 with max 707/733, and
    parameters 5/5 with max 11/11.

evidence E_POSTGRES:
  |
    Repository-scoped secdat supplied DATABASE_URL, DIRECT_URL, and
    SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF without exposing values. DIRECT_URL selected an IPv6
    route unavailable from this WSL host, while DATABASE_URL passed strict CA
    verification and reported database CREATE privilege. For this isolated
    verification invocation only, DATABASE_URL was also supplied as the
    administrator URL. The live smoke applied every migration including 0024,
    passed authentication and repository checks, and removed its unique schema.
    Readback found zero kshiai_smoke schemas and neither B4 table in public.

evidence E_RCA:
  |
    Separate command-line LLMTHINK audits with no fatal, error, or warning
    findings established and corrected three smoke blockers: incomplete
    namespace isolation for unqualified migration objects, blank optional
    POSTGRES_CA_CERT_PATH being treated as a real path, and a legacy-compatible
    smoke fixture omitting the current required basicAttack. The runner now sets
    its session search_path to the unique schema, blank CA overrides select the
    bundled verified CA with four regression tests, and new smoke characters are
    explicitly CombatReadyCharacterSheet values.

premise LIMIT:
  |
    Isolated live application does not apply migration 0024 to public or prove a
    production rollout. These results do not establish B5 semantic operations,
    provider behavior, candidates, acceptance, activation, policy cutover,
    production migration, deployment, or restored characters.

decision D1 based_on P1, E_CONTRACT, E_PERSISTENCE, E_FIXTURES, E_GATES, E_POSTGRES, E_RCA, LIMIT:
  |
    Treat cb204 B4 as implemented and verified locally plus an isolated live
    PostgreSQL application. Permit cb205 B5 semantic generation, review, and
    repair implementation to remain the next plan candidate; preserve production,
    provider, migration, deployment, and activation gates.
